Chapter: TextAppendAlias

  cites Foreword chapter Sha256
  cites Foreword chapter Console

 Regression for a silent miscompile: a heap string with spare buffer
 capacity (e.g. sha256-to-hex output) must NOT be mutated by a later
 text-append. The buggy __str_concat fast path extended the left
 operand's buffer in place and overwrote its length when it ended at
 the heap top, corrupting still-live aliases (val BareMetalMiscompiles
 Bug 2: hash-pw's `salt & ":" & pw` corrupted `salt`).

Section: Body

  str-bytes-loop : Text, Integer, Integer, List Integer -> List Integer
  str-bytes-loop (s) (i) (n) (acc) =
    if i >= n then acc
    else str-bytes-loop s (i + 1) n (list-push acc (char-code (char-at s i)))

  digest : Text -> Text
  digest (t) = sha256-to-hex (sha256 (str-bytes-loop t 0 (text-length t) []))

  opening : [Console] Nothing = act
    let a = digest "x"
    in let b = a & "Z"
    in print-line-uni (if text-length a == 64 then "PASS" else "FAIL len=" & show (text-length a))
  end

